>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `quickcheck`

``` hol4
Refute.quickcheck : term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runs Refute's Quickcheck backends.

`Refute.quickcheck tm` is `refute_with [upd_search QuickcheckBackends] tm`:
the `exhaustive`, `random`, and `narrowing` backends run with every
other field of `!Refute.the_config`, including substrate, size,
iterations, seed, certification, quiet mode, and expectations.

The exhaustive and random backends need an executable goal and use the
substrate the configuration selects.  Narrowing accepts any goal, so it
may be the only backend that applies; a counterexample it finds records
`"narrowing"` as its backend.  The `kodkod` model finder is not
selected; use [`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute) for that.

